WEBVTT

01:22.747 --> 01:26.959
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:32.924 --> 01:36.010
This one isn't dead. Just paralyzed.

01:36.093 --> 01:38.429
On this floor, of all places?
Can you revive him?

01:38.512 --> 01:39.764
Not sure.

01:50.316 --> 01:52.902
Good. Looks like you're revived.

01:56.447 --> 01:59.742
We were wiped out?

02:00.868 --> 02:02.119
My necklace is gone.

02:02.954 --> 02:04.497
My coins are gone, too.

02:04.580 --> 02:06.624
And so are all the jewels.

02:07.291 --> 02:09.669
We lost some of our belongings.

02:09.752 --> 02:11.087
Do you know anything about it?

02:11.671 --> 02:13.881
No doubt about it.
They were taken out by Treasure Bugs.

02:13.965 --> 02:14.799
Shh!

02:14.882 --> 02:16.759
Nah, we don't know a thing.

02:16.842 --> 02:19.845
We found you all
lined up nicely on the ground.

02:19.929 --> 02:23.599
Some folks must have
passed here before we did.

02:24.892 --> 02:25.935
A strand of hair.

02:26.978 --> 02:28.604
It's magic to ward off ghosts.

02:29.105 --> 02:31.691
Someone definitely
came in contact with us.

02:34.944 --> 02:35.861
An elf…

02:36.445 --> 02:37.863
A tall-man…

02:38.447 --> 02:41.367
A half-foot… And a dwarf.

02:42.076 --> 02:44.120
They had a meal here.

02:44.203 --> 02:45.705
A meal?

02:45.788 --> 02:47.498
They sure have some nerve.

02:47.581 --> 02:48.499
Let's go after them.

02:48.582 --> 02:50.084
Hold up.

02:51.210 --> 02:52.628
We're not a charity, you know.

02:55.715 --> 02:56.632
Here.

02:56.716 --> 02:57.883
Thanks.

03:00.469 --> 03:02.138
Why didn't you tell them?

03:02.221 --> 03:03.597
It's simple.

03:03.681 --> 03:05.975
The more corpses, the better.

03:11.647 --> 03:13.899
I really want to wash my hair soon.

03:13.983 --> 03:15.901
You'll feel refreshed
if you crop your hair.

03:15.985 --> 03:18.696
There you go again, saying mean things.

03:19.196 --> 03:21.699
Don't you want
to wash your beard as well, Senshi?

03:23.492 --> 03:25.578
How long has it been
since you last washed it?

03:25.661 --> 03:26.996
Let's give it a wash right now!

03:28.080 --> 03:30.916
Your hair plays an important role
in magic, too.

03:31.000 --> 03:34.670
Taking care of it is like warm-up.

03:34.754 --> 03:38.591
With your beard like that,
my support magic might not work on you.

03:38.674 --> 03:40.051
That would be just great.

03:40.634 --> 03:43.429
Right! I have really nice soap.

03:44.013 --> 03:46.599
I'll wash your beard with it and braid it!

03:49.852 --> 03:51.937
Huh? I can't find it.

03:53.647 --> 03:55.816
Right, that day…

03:55.900 --> 03:59.028
No way! It was so expensive, though!

03:59.111 --> 04:00.321
Let's go.

04:01.697 --> 04:03.074
On the fourth basement floor,

04:03.657 --> 04:06.243
<c.bg_transparent><i>there is a lake formed
by underground water</i></c.bg_transparent>

04:06.327 --> 04:08.287
flowing through carved-out bedrock.

04:09.455 --> 04:12.833
<c.bg_transparent><i>The magic-infused water
emits a faint glow,</i></c.bg_transparent>

04:12.917 --> 04:15.419
and far in the depths of the water,

04:15.503 --> 04:17.838
<c.bg_transparent><i>the castle town can be seen
like a wavering illusion.</i></c.bg_transparent>

04:19.006 --> 04:22.093
How do you usually explore
the fourth floor, Senshi?

04:22.176 --> 04:25.763
I fish and set traps around here.

04:25.846 --> 04:27.264
That's about it.

04:27.807 --> 04:30.101
How do you fellows get through this place?

04:30.684 --> 04:32.978
With magic, of course.

04:33.562 --> 04:35.564
I use this to do this and…

04:36.857 --> 04:37.858
There!

04:39.860 --> 04:42.029
We walk across on water.

04:42.113 --> 04:44.198
N…

04:44.281 --> 04:45.116
N…?

04:45.199 --> 04:47.118
No!

04:47.201 --> 04:49.245
No!

04:49.328 --> 04:50.871
-No!
-No need to get so upset.

04:50.955 --> 04:53.082
-No!
-This won't work.

04:53.165 --> 04:55.000
Let's tie a rope around him
and drag him along.

04:55.084 --> 04:56.127
No.

04:56.210 --> 04:58.838
Put a spell on him
while I'm holding him down.

04:58.921 --> 05:00.589
-What?
-With his armor--

05:01.090 --> 05:04.385
With his armor, it's the only way
to get him across the water.

05:04.468 --> 05:06.387
It's too dangerous to take a boat.

05:07.680 --> 05:10.266
People easily fall for the path of ease.

05:10.349 --> 05:13.853
It takes only a moment to get rusty,
but it takes a long, long time to--

05:13.936 --> 05:14.770
There!

05:16.105 --> 05:18.149
See? It wasn't such a big deal, was it?

05:18.232 --> 05:19.525
Y-You…!

05:20.109 --> 05:23.654
I don't get it.
Why do you hate magic so much?

05:23.737 --> 05:27.324
You people are too casual
when it comes to using magic.

05:27.408 --> 05:29.285
That's something I don't understand.

05:29.368 --> 05:30.870
Now, now.

05:30.953 --> 05:32.413
What's done is done.

05:32.997 --> 05:35.040
You might actually like it.

05:38.836 --> 05:39.670
-Huh?
-Huh?

05:40.296 --> 05:41.338
W-Why?

05:41.422 --> 05:43.424
Why isn't my magic working
as well as it should?

05:43.507 --> 05:44.925
This must be it.

05:45.009 --> 05:46.802
Ugh, is this an insulator?

05:47.386 --> 05:49.847
It's soaked with the oils
and blood of various monsters.

05:49.930 --> 05:50.973
Ew!

05:51.056 --> 05:52.433
Wash it off quickly!

05:52.516 --> 05:54.476
I'm not sure
if it will come off with just water…

05:54.560 --> 05:55.853
No need.

05:56.645 --> 05:59.815
I will get across the water in my own way.

05:59.899 --> 06:01.066
Huh?

06:01.150 --> 06:02.443
Are you gonna build a boat?

06:02.526 --> 06:04.069
You'll sink like a stone in no time.

06:04.153 --> 06:07.615
No, he must have some amazing plan.

06:07.698 --> 06:09.783
You sure have a lot of confidence in him.

06:09.867 --> 06:11.076
I don't get it.

06:11.660 --> 06:12.578
Watch me.

06:14.914 --> 06:17.208
-Is that the outer shell of a Mimic?
-Shh!

06:30.804 --> 06:32.097
A Kelpie!

06:32.181 --> 06:33.807
Watch out! Get back!

06:33.891 --> 06:35.809
It's fine. It's harmless.

06:36.810 --> 06:40.439
Anne is a horse
that always shows up whenever I fish.

06:40.522 --> 06:41.357
Anne?

06:41.941 --> 06:45.861
For a while now, I've been wondering
if I could use her to get across the lake.

06:45.945 --> 06:47.238
-What?
-What?

06:47.321 --> 06:51.367
Perhaps I can use the Mimic's shell
to steer her somehow.

06:51.450 --> 06:54.245
T-That's…

06:54.328 --> 06:55.829
so cool!

06:55.913 --> 06:56.872
THIS SCREAMS ADVENTURE

06:56.956 --> 06:58.374
I'm against it.

06:58.999 --> 07:03.003
I think it'd be more practical
to use its guts to make a float.

07:03.087 --> 07:05.172
H-How can you say that?

07:05.256 --> 07:07.132
How cruel of you!

07:07.716 --> 07:09.260
Monsters are dangerous.

07:09.343 --> 07:11.512
Especially ones that are charming.

07:12.096 --> 07:15.140
Kelpies make you lower your guard
and entice you into the water.

07:15.766 --> 07:18.519
You can never know
what's going on in a monster's mind.

07:18.602 --> 07:22.356
I've known Anne for a long time,
just like I've known the golems.

07:22.439 --> 07:25.025
I know her much better than you.

07:27.111 --> 07:29.446
Why does everyone
have a soft spot for mammals

07:29.530 --> 07:32.449
when they won't let me grow
a Man-eating Plant?

07:32.950 --> 07:35.369
Do you really not know why?

07:35.869 --> 07:38.038
Let's go, Anne!

07:43.127 --> 07:44.545
-Senshi!
-Senshi!

07:44.628 --> 07:45.713
-Marcille!
-Huh?

07:54.597 --> 07:55.681
Anne…

08:02.021 --> 08:03.439
Stop it, Anne!

08:08.736 --> 08:09.612
Laios!

08:14.033 --> 08:15.326
Forgive me, Anne.

08:23.876 --> 08:25.085
No way.

08:25.169 --> 08:27.129
No way!

08:27.671 --> 08:29.590
Please no!

08:37.931 --> 08:40.601
So, she was waiting for me
to get on her back?

08:41.185 --> 08:43.812
But she could've attacked me
whenever she wanted.

08:43.896 --> 08:44.772
I don't know.

08:45.314 --> 08:48.067
There's no knowing
what a monster is thinking.

08:49.735 --> 08:50.778
I don't understand.

08:51.403 --> 08:52.571
I don't understand at all.

08:58.285 --> 08:59.370
You must be cold.

08:59.453 --> 09:01.497
I'll start a fire right now.

09:02.831 --> 09:03.957
Hey!

09:04.625 --> 09:07.127
You were that fond of her,
and now you're going to eat her?

09:07.878 --> 09:09.338
Unbelievable.

09:09.421 --> 09:10.381
Why, though?

09:11.423 --> 09:12.424
Can I help?

09:13.592 --> 09:14.635
No.

09:15.302 --> 09:16.970
I'll do it on my own.

09:23.769 --> 09:24.645
Hey.

09:25.229 --> 09:28.399
Can I get some of the fat?

09:29.024 --> 09:31.235
What brought this on?

09:33.237 --> 09:34.571
Just an idea.

09:39.993 --> 09:42.579
What on earth are we doing here?

09:43.080 --> 09:43.997
Chilchuck.

09:44.498 --> 09:46.959
Something is floating over there.

09:47.042 --> 09:48.502
It better not be people.

09:48.585 --> 09:49.628
Let's go and take a look.

09:49.712 --> 09:51.755
What? I'd rather not.

09:56.135 --> 09:58.011
What are these white things?

09:58.095 --> 09:59.096
It's grain.

09:59.179 --> 10:00.931
Looks like it's been spilled.

10:01.515 --> 10:02.975
And here are the owners.

10:04.017 --> 10:05.894
Let's draw them out of the water.

10:06.729 --> 10:07.688
What is it?

10:07.771 --> 10:10.691
Doesn't his face seem familiar?

10:10.774 --> 10:11.692
Nope.

10:12.234 --> 10:14.570
Oh, I know this kobold!

10:14.653 --> 10:16.739
We found him dead
on the third basement floor.

10:16.822 --> 10:18.907
How did they get ahead of us?

10:26.623 --> 10:28.333
So, they met a Mermaid
and killed each other.

10:28.917 --> 10:30.919
The poor… things…

10:35.090 --> 10:36.049
Chilchuck?

10:36.967 --> 10:38.844
Chil! Chilchuck!

10:41.430 --> 10:42.681
Chil!

11:15.088 --> 11:17.591
They never let me finish the song,

11:17.674 --> 11:19.676
even though
I took the trouble of remembering it.

11:22.721 --> 11:24.389
That should do it.

11:25.766 --> 11:28.185
We shouldn't let
the scattered grain go to waste.

11:28.268 --> 11:29.561
Let's gather the grain for them.

11:29.645 --> 11:31.146
That's going too far.

11:31.230 --> 11:33.190
Then let's take them for ourselves.

11:33.273 --> 11:34.942
It'll make Marcille happy.

11:35.025 --> 11:36.777
Poor Marcille.

11:41.990 --> 11:43.075
No!

11:43.659 --> 11:44.993
I didn't say anything yet.

11:45.077 --> 11:47.955
You promised not to go for demi-humans!

11:48.038 --> 11:50.958
Demi-humans…

11:51.542 --> 11:53.085
What are they?

11:53.168 --> 11:54.211
What do you mean?

11:54.294 --> 11:56.213
Mermaids come in different forms.

11:56.296 --> 11:58.215
<c.bg_transparent><i>Some are mammals,
while others are more like fish.</i></c.bg_transparent>

11:58.799 --> 12:00.259
This one's in the fish category.

12:00.342 --> 12:02.678
It lays eggs, so it doesn't have
a belly button or nipples.

12:02.761 --> 12:03.720
Instead, it has gills.

12:04.304 --> 12:07.683
They're farther removed
from humans than cows or pigs.

12:08.725 --> 12:09.643
What?

12:10.686 --> 12:13.105
-No way!
-What?!

12:13.188 --> 12:14.982
Why, though?

12:15.065 --> 12:17.609
Why can we eat cow but not a Fish-man?

12:17.693 --> 12:19.611
It just doesn't feel right.

12:20.195 --> 12:21.613
Feel?

12:22.906 --> 12:23.949
Feel, huh?

12:27.452 --> 12:28.829
They're still at it.

12:29.371 --> 12:31.790
I'm starting to feel hungry,
so how about we whip something up?

12:33.125 --> 12:35.377
<c.bg_transparent><i>Throw the grains in water
and put it over a fire.</i></c.bg_transparent>

12:35.460 --> 12:38.255
<c.bg_transparent><i>Toss in some flaked Mimic
and waterweeds, then--</i></c.bg_transparent>

12:38.338 --> 12:39.631
Wait a minute.

12:39.715 --> 12:42.009
That's the stuff that was growing
on the Fish-man's head.

12:42.092 --> 12:45.512
Yeah, but this is just a normal plant.

12:45.596 --> 12:47.764
The Fish-men use it to camouflage.

12:48.348 --> 12:51.310
Without it, they'd look even more fishy.

12:52.603 --> 12:54.605
Does it still upset your feelings?

12:54.688 --> 12:56.648
This is starting to become a bother.

12:57.232 --> 12:59.401
Fine. Have it your way.

13:01.987 --> 13:05.157
<c.bg_transparent><i>I think I might've made
an error in judgment just now.</i></c.bg_transparent>

13:05.240 --> 13:06.742
All right. It's ready.

13:06.825 --> 13:09.161
PORRIDGE WITH SCATTERED BARLEY

13:09.745 --> 13:11.997
Marcille, Senshi, let's have lunch.

13:12.497 --> 13:14.249
Is it that time already?

13:14.333 --> 13:16.668
Where did you manage to find some grains?

13:16.752 --> 13:19.379
I scavenged them
from the fallen adventurers over there.

13:19.463 --> 13:20.922
What on earth were you thinking?

13:22.257 --> 13:24.676
<c.bg_transparent><i>Good question.
I knew Marcille wouldn't disappoint.</i></c.bg_transparent>

13:24.760 --> 13:27.262
But you already cooked them, so.

13:27.929 --> 13:29.264
I'll dig right in!

13:37.022 --> 13:39.232
Hmm, there's a pop in the texture.

13:39.316 --> 13:40.609
What is it?

13:40.692 --> 13:41.902
Probably fish eggs.

13:41.985 --> 13:43.987
They must've been on the water weeds.

13:45.280 --> 13:46.239
It tastes good.

13:46.323 --> 13:48.200
I know, right?

13:48.283 --> 13:49.785
I'm glad I added them.

13:50.410 --> 13:51.453
Come with me.

13:52.120 --> 13:52.954
Hey!

13:53.038 --> 13:55.248
Those were a Fish-man's eggs,
weren't they?

13:55.332 --> 13:57.876
I've heard Fish-men have
a habit of laying their eggs on waterweeds

13:57.959 --> 14:00.462
that they wear on their heads
to protect them or something!

14:01.129 --> 14:02.172
What's the matter?

14:02.923 --> 14:03.924
Marcille.

14:05.926 --> 14:07.844
Does it taste good?

14:10.931 --> 14:11.890
Yeah!

14:17.187 --> 14:18.105
Senshi.

14:19.523 --> 14:20.857
This is for you.

14:21.692 --> 14:24.611
I made soap using the Kelpie's fat.

14:25.195 --> 14:28.281
Kelpie's fat is often used as hair oil,

14:28.365 --> 14:30.367
but it can also be used
for clothes and dishes.

14:33.453 --> 14:35.664
Can I use it right now?

14:35.747 --> 14:38.375
It's still being saponified,
so I'm not sure.

14:38.959 --> 14:40.252
I want to give it a try.

14:40.335 --> 14:42.129
You put a lot of effort
into making it, right?

14:43.964 --> 14:44.965
Okay.

15:24.379 --> 15:26.423
Thank goodness!

15:26.506 --> 15:28.550
Now, we can move ahead together.

15:29.843 --> 15:31.094
I see.

15:31.178 --> 15:33.889
Now that it's come to this,
I've realized something.

15:34.890 --> 15:38.810
Walking on water
actually feels quite nice.

15:39.853 --> 15:41.938
Thank you, Marcille.

15:44.274 --> 15:47.319
Some soap got into my eye.

15:59.414 --> 16:00.373
Leave this to me.

16:00.916 --> 16:02.834
I'll wipe them out!

16:02.918 --> 16:04.086
Don't!

16:09.591 --> 16:11.259
-Watch out!
-Ow!

16:13.720 --> 16:15.263
I told you not to!

16:15.347 --> 16:17.849
An underwater explosion
kills too many of them!

16:17.933 --> 16:18.767
What?

16:19.351 --> 16:22.687
These Blade Fish can be stewed,
grilled, steamed,

16:22.771 --> 16:25.357
dried, smoked, or eaten raw.

16:25.440 --> 16:27.776
They're delicious
no matter how you prepare them.

16:28.443 --> 16:30.821
But they're a food source
for other monsters as well.

16:30.904 --> 16:35.033
If their population decreases,
it could disrupt the dungeon's ecosystem.

16:35.117 --> 16:37.702
So you should get them one at a time.

16:37.786 --> 16:40.163
What? You're asking too much!

16:40.747 --> 16:41.748
Now that I think about it,

16:41.832 --> 16:44.417
it seems like there are fewer
mid-sized monsters around than usual.

16:44.501 --> 16:45.418
See?

16:45.502 --> 16:48.130
I can't just go easy on them, though.

16:48.213 --> 16:50.048
Not when they're trying to kill us.

16:50.632 --> 16:53.552
If anything,
there are more Blade Fish than usual.

16:53.635 --> 16:55.679
I don't think there's anything
to be concerned about.

16:55.762 --> 16:57.806
But what if the monsters end up starving?

16:57.889 --> 17:00.934
I don't want to die
just to protect their ecosystem!

17:05.772 --> 17:08.483
You people are too quick
to take the easy path.

17:09.025 --> 17:12.696
What? Then you should try
taking them out one by one.

17:12.779 --> 17:13.864
It's hard, you know!

17:15.782 --> 17:18.410
You should think about the ecosystem more…

17:20.996 --> 17:22.706
What's going on?

17:22.789 --> 17:23.874
Senshi!

17:26.126 --> 17:28.795
What was that all about?
They just passed by us.

17:29.671 --> 17:30.714
Are you hurt?

17:32.424 --> 17:33.425
Senshi?

17:35.135 --> 17:36.803
Something is approaching.

17:36.887 --> 17:37.888
What?

17:45.395 --> 17:47.314
You're kidding, right?

17:48.231 --> 17:49.566
It's way too huge!

17:59.576 --> 18:00.702
A squid?

18:00.785 --> 18:02.412
Or is it an octopus?

18:02.495 --> 18:03.705
It's a Kraken!

18:03.788 --> 18:06.416
It's a big monster to begin with,

18:06.499 --> 18:08.668
but this one's a few times larger
than the usual ones!

18:09.669 --> 18:11.087
It's so cool!

18:11.171 --> 18:12.631
What do we do?

18:12.714 --> 18:14.507
If we act rashly, it's gonna get us!

18:14.591 --> 18:16.009
We'll draw its attention!

18:16.509 --> 18:17.719
I'm counting on you, Marcille.

18:18.762 --> 18:20.222
Magic again?

18:20.305 --> 18:23.099
Relax. I'll strike it this time.

18:26.811 --> 18:27.729
Here it comes!

18:28.605 --> 18:29.898
Don't stop running!

18:37.614 --> 18:38.448
Right there!

18:41.117 --> 18:42.410
I did it!

18:50.877 --> 18:53.296
No way! It didn't take a hit!

18:54.965 --> 18:58.009
Using a weapon on it will only
slice through its outer skin at most.

19:16.695 --> 19:18.613
There must be magic I can use…

19:18.697 --> 19:19.990
Marcille!

19:20.073 --> 19:22.742
-Use your magic again.
-What?

19:22.826 --> 19:25.328
I can't pull off such a powerful magic
in quick succession.

19:25.412 --> 19:26.246
No.

19:26.913 --> 19:27.831
This will do.

19:28.999 --> 19:31.751
I mean, this is your first encounter
with a Kraken, right?

19:32.877 --> 19:34.921
Do you even know
what kind of monster it is?

19:35.005 --> 19:36.381
-I don't.
-What?

19:36.965 --> 19:38.550
I don't know much about Krakens,

19:38.633 --> 19:41.136
but I have cleaned
squids and octopuses before.

19:43.096 --> 19:44.014
Watch out, Marcille!

19:44.097 --> 19:45.265
It's heading your way!

19:48.268 --> 19:50.645
Water-Walk!

20:05.452 --> 20:07.537
To kill a squid or an octopus,

20:07.620 --> 20:09.789
stab it right between the eyes!

20:21.384 --> 20:22.802
Amazing.

20:23.720 --> 20:24.554
Huh?

20:24.637 --> 20:25.847
Where's Laios?

20:27.015 --> 20:30.310
Hey. I'm over here.

20:32.979 --> 20:36.441
Looks like this creature was devouring
all the medium-sized monsters.

20:37.108 --> 20:39.652
Both of you, come here.

20:42.155 --> 20:45.450
You should try cleaning a cephalopod
at least once.

20:46.659 --> 20:49.829
Stab squids and octopuses here
to kill them neatly.

20:49.913 --> 20:52.082
Do squids and octopuses taste good?

20:52.165 --> 20:54.542
No way! You've never tried them?

20:54.626 --> 20:56.586
They taste really good, you know!

20:56.669 --> 21:01.216
You can stew, grill, steam, dry, smoke,
or even enjoy them raw.

21:01.299 --> 21:04.094
They really taste great
no matter how you cook them!

21:04.677 --> 21:07.847
I know a good place,
so I'll show you there next time.

21:07.931 --> 21:09.265
Can't I try one now?

21:10.809 --> 21:12.102
I dug my own grave!

21:12.811 --> 21:15.105
Wow, this is so weird!

21:15.188 --> 21:17.107
How do I eat this?

21:17.190 --> 21:19.359
Let's try salting it.

21:22.570 --> 21:24.489
-It stinks.
-Well, well!

21:25.073 --> 21:26.533
It tastes awfully bitter.

21:26.616 --> 21:28.743
It's making my mouth tingle.

21:28.827 --> 21:31.621
Marcille, do you really
eat this in various dishes?

21:31.704 --> 21:34.624
No, I don't!
That's a weird misunderstanding!

21:45.135 --> 21:46.761
How marvelous!

21:46.845 --> 21:49.681
A big parasite for a big monster!

21:49.764 --> 21:51.891
Ew, disgusting!

21:51.975 --> 21:53.059
Throw it away now!

21:53.643 --> 21:54.894
What's all the fuss about?

21:54.978 --> 21:57.313
Most creatures
have parasitic worms inside them.

21:57.397 --> 22:00.775
And many of them end up in our meals, too.

22:00.859 --> 22:02.444
You didn't have to tell me that!

22:03.027 --> 22:05.321
Well, if we cook it,
we should be able to eat this as well.

22:05.405 --> 22:06.489
No!

22:06.573 --> 22:08.783
That's one way of looking at it.

22:08.867 --> 22:10.577
I said no!

22:28.219 --> 22:31.139
Let's try broiling these with some sauce.

22:35.810 --> 22:38.646
It's upsetting how amazing it smells!

22:47.113 --> 22:48.364
It's done!

22:48.448 --> 22:51.034
BROILED AND GLAZED
GIANT PARASITIC WORM

22:56.873 --> 22:58.124
It's good!

22:58.708 --> 23:02.128
I can't quite put it into words,
but it's really soft and delicious!

23:02.212 --> 23:04.964
It's got a bit of a slime,
but it's quite meaty.

23:08.426 --> 23:10.303
I-It's good.

23:10.386 --> 23:11.471
Not bad.

23:12.055 --> 23:15.266
This has a delicious taste
that's unlike your typical fish.

23:15.350 --> 23:17.602
Isn't it even better
than squid or octopus?

23:17.685 --> 23:19.604
That's not…

23:20.730 --> 23:22.857
true, probably.

23:22.941 --> 23:26.402
I'm pretty sure this would be delicious,
no matter how you prepare it as well.

23:26.486 --> 23:28.780
I had a bite of it raw,
but it went down nicely.

23:28.863 --> 23:30.615
Hold on, you ate it raw?

23:31.199 --> 23:32.242
Just a little.

23:32.325 --> 23:34.077
It was already dead, so it should be fine.

23:35.954 --> 23:37.872
The fish are eating the Kraken.

23:37.956 --> 23:42.377
That should help the medium-sized monsters
slowly come back.

23:45.964 --> 23:47.382
My stomach…

23:48.925 --> 23:50.385
Ow…

23:50.468 --> 23:52.762
What's the matter? Are you okay?

23:52.845 --> 23:53.972
Well, well…

23:54.472 --> 23:56.349
It's just as I thought.

23:56.432 --> 24:00.895
Laios, what you have is the parasite
that was inside the giant parasitic worm.

24:02.480 --> 24:05.233
<c.bg_transparent><i>It's the same kind
you find in your average fish, too.</i></c.bg_transparent>

24:05.316 --> 24:07.110
<c.bg_transparent><i>I spotted one
when I was cleaning the big worm.</i></c.bg_transparent>

24:07.193 --> 24:08.152
It can't be…

24:08.736 --> 24:10.280
It won't parasite on a human,

24:10.363 --> 24:13.157
but it does make a hole in your stomach,
which can be very painful.

24:13.241 --> 24:15.994
All you can do is wait for it to die.

24:16.995 --> 24:19.664
I think I might die first.

24:19.747 --> 24:22.208
Why not throw a healing spell
on him every now and then?

24:22.292 --> 24:23.418
Good idea.

24:23.501 --> 24:25.545
But I see now.

24:26.087 --> 24:28.298
The Fish-men eat the Blade Fish,

24:28.381 --> 24:30.633
and the Kraken eats the Fish-men.

24:30.717 --> 24:33.011
We took down the Kraken,

24:33.094 --> 24:35.054
and the little fish feast on its flesh.

24:35.763 --> 24:38.975
<c.bg_transparent><i>Laios ate the parasitic worm
inside the Kraken,</i></c.bg_transparent>

24:39.058 --> 24:42.312
<c.bg_transparent><i>and the parasite within that worm
ended up poking a hole in Laios' stomach.</i></c.bg_transparent>

24:43.771 --> 24:48.484
I guess it was a little arrogant of me
to try to protect the ecosystem.

24:48.568 --> 24:53.573
Right from the start, we were already
a part of the dungeon's circle of life.

24:55.533 --> 24:57.577
Laios attempted to speak,

24:57.660 --> 25:02.582
<c.bg_transparent><i>but the excruciating pain and nausea
left his mind completely empty.</i></c.bg_transparent>

25:03.499 --> 25:07.420
<c.bg_transparent><i>The agony, which felt as if knives
were slicing through his insides,</i></c.bg_transparent>

25:07.503 --> 25:08.671
persisted all night.

25:09.672 --> 25:14.260
<c.bg_transparent><i>And he vowed
never to eat a parasitic worm raw again.</i></c.bg_transparent>

26:41.973 --> 26:46.144
Subtitle translation by: Ai Matsuoka
